{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"8c2f5d3b8941526fc57209109c4a0627cfaf9fd4ce1ad9848c66ceaf4a9d9987","digest":{"component_or_area":"Gerrit CI verification workflow","key_entities":[".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py","scripts/check_wall_clock_asserts.py","verify job","gate step"],"problem_keywords":["ci gate script missing","workflow definition skew","pre-gate changes fail","tree mismatch","gate step hard failure"],"propositions":["Newly landed gate steps invoke repo scripts unconditionally, causing hard failures on changes whose base predates the gate-introducing commit because the script does not exist in the checked-out tree.","Gerrit CI's model uses workflow definition from target branch but checks out the change's tree, creating a legitimate divergence window that gate steps must tolerate.","Gate steps must skip with an explanatory message when their script is absent from the checked-out tree, and execute normally when present.","The existence-check idiom and rationale for definition-from-target-branch versus change tree skew must be documented inline in the workflow to guide future gate authors."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787657545283144001,"uuid":"f829ead6-4c54-44e1-9e8c-ecfb76b844ed"}